              {
                "text": "**Analyzing Grid Relationships**\n\nI'm examining the structure of these 8x4 grids. Right now, I'm focusing on the relationship between the top and bottom 4x4 subgrids. I noticed the top half is always green (colors 0 and 3), and the bottom half is always blue (colors 0 and 1). The target output is a red (color 2) 4x4 grid. I'm starting to consider how the inputs relate to generate the output.\n\n\n**Confirming a Zero-Based Rule**\n\nI've tested the hypothesis on a new example. My analysis indicates that the red \"2\" appears precisely where both the top and bottom grid elements are zero. This holds true for the test data; the previous examples I was looking at. The zeros in the source determine the position of the 2's in the output.\n\n\n",
